        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.184,
            0.069,
            0.488,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Manjari | Grade 9 | Part I"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.107,
            0.886,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": "7. The village playground is shaped as a square of side 40 metres. A path of width s metres is created around the playground for people to walk. Find an expression for the area of the path in terms of s."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.145,
            0.188,
            0.824,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": "8. If a number plus its reciprocal equals $\\frac { 1 0 } { 3 }$ , find the number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.226,
            0.885,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": "9. A rectangular pool has area $2 x ^ { 2 } + 7 x + 3$ square hastas. If its width is $2 x + 1$ hastas, find its length. Hasta was a unit used to measure length."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.29,
            0.874,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "\\*10. If both $x - 2$ and $x - { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } }$ are factors of $p x ^ { 2 } + 5 x + r ,$ , show that $p _ { \\leq } r$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.336,
            0.74,
            0.376
          ],
          "content": "\\*11. If $a+b+c=5$ and ab $+bc+ca=10$ , then prove that $a^{3}+b^{3}+c^{3}-3abc=-25.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.122,
            0.383,
            0.884,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "\\*12. By factoring the expression, check that $n ^ { 3 } - n$ is always divisible by 6 for all natural numbers n. Give reasons."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.43,
            0.376,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": "\\*13. Find the value of"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.455,
            0.602,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "(i) $x^{3}+y^{3}-12xy+64,\\mathrm{when}\\ x+y=-4$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.478,
            0.622,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $x^{3}-8y^{3}-36xy-216,\\mathrm{when}\\ x=2y+6$"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.374,
            0.525,
            0.633,
            0.547
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Chapter summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.567,
            0.884,
            0.609
          ],
          "content": "**Identities** are equations that are true for all values of the variables."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.616,
            0.885,
            0.658
          ],
          "content": "One of the ways to visualise identities is using geometrical models or algebra tiles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.666,
            0.813,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": "• Identities can also be used to factor algebraic expressions."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.695,
            0.885,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": "Factorisation of quadratic expressions may be visualised by means of algebra tiles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.745,
            0.885,
            0.788
          ],
          "content": "• Identities can also be used to simplify calculations such as squaring numbers or evaluating products of numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.795,
            0.886,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": "Rational algebraic expressions may be simplified by factorisation and removing the common factors in the numerator and denominator, provided such a factor exists and it is not equal to zero."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
